/T (Example and application: To grow as a software engineer, I can set a weekly target such as finishing ten C programs. Using N-Ach thinking, the target must be challenging but realistic, progress must be measured and feedback must be reviewed. Each week I can compare the first and the last attempt, note what improved and decide the next target. Over months, these small, visible improvements will turn into strong technical fundamentals and the confidence to join hackathons and coding clubs.)
