/Title (Course details: The course links mindset closely with habits, which are automatic responses set off by our surroundings. Good habits take steady effort to build, while bad ones slip in easily through peer influence and leave a lasting mark on character. The habit cycle runs from a thought or trigger to an action, then a reward or penalty, then repetition until it becomes a habit; habits shape character, and character decides success or failure. Examples from R.K. Narayan's The Guide and William Golding's Lord of the Flies show that both our darker impulses and our power to choose better ones live inside us.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3722 0 R
/Prev 3742 0 R
/Next 3781 0 R
>>
endobj
