/Title (technical knowledge is put to use in study, work and daily life. Communication, listening, responsibility and teamwork are presented as the core of professional behaviour. The lecture makes the point that technical ability alone is not enough: explaining a solution accurately, receiving criticism honestly and staying calm inside a team are practical signs of professional growth. Course details: The course stresses that soft skills cannot be memorised for show; they grow through practice and a real change in behaviour. It points out that relationships account for most of our happiness, and it borrows Stephen Covey's habit of beginning with the end in mind, so that each day's tasks are judged against long-term goals and habits that add nothing are dropped. Using well-known optical illustrations, it also shows how two people can look at the same thing and see different realities, and it advises seeking to understand others before expecting them to understand us.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3736 0 R
/Prev 3754 0 R
/Next 3803 0 R
>>
endobj
