/Title (Course details: Feedback can only help when it is actually received, which is why the course gives so much attention to listening. Listening is described as an active, deliberate effort that is quite different from merely hearing, and it follows seven stages: reception, selection, organisation, assimilation, interpretation, evaluation and response. Noise, physical discomfort, prejudice, half-attention and emotional bias get in the way, and the remedies are full-body attentiveness, empathy and a sensible use of silence. The course also reminds learners that procrastination is mainly the difficulty of starting; once a task is begun, the urge to finish carries us forward.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 3745 0 R
/Prev 3764 0 R
/Next 3809 0 R
>>
